      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is given by $⟨x,y⟩=4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ Find $⟨x,y⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =4{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-3)\\cdot 0+3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot 0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =0-12+0 \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
